958
01:12:11,227 --> 01:12:13,627
We're movin'.

959
01:12:17,500 --> 01:12:20,936
Check it out.

960
01:12:27,711 --> 01:12:30,908
Ah!

961
01:12:39,189 --> 01:12:43,455
Bock, do something. This is too much.
Sam, what are you doing?

962
01:12:43,560 --> 01:12:45,960
Whoo!

963
01:12:48,398 --> 01:12:50,366
Ohh!

964
01:12:55,605 --> 01:12:57,869
Put me down, James.
I'm not four years old.

965
01:12:57,974 --> 01:12:59,942
Put me down. I can walk.

966
01:13:00,043 --> 01:13:01,476
Yeah. The thing is, you can't.

967
01:13:01,578 --> 01:13:03,512
So why don't you just let me
help you, Samantha?

968
01:13:03,613 --> 01:13:06,207
Why should I trust you?

969
01:13:06,316 --> 01:13:09,251
You lied to me.
You made me like you.

970
01:13:09,352 --> 01:13:11,286
Why are you a Secret Service agent?

971
01:13:11,388 --> 01:13:14,846
Honestly, right now I'm just tryin'
to get through this and do my job.

972
01:13:14,958 --> 01:13:19,019
- Which, by the way, you're
making very difficult. - Oh. Really?

973
01:13:21,631 --> 01:13:26,034
Why are you doin' this, Sam?
This isn't you.

974
01:13:30,373 --> 01:13:33,274
Whoo! This is me, James...

975
01:13:33,376 --> 01:13:37,472
me without you.

976
01:14:03,973 --> 01:14:05,873
What was that?

977
01:14:07,677 --> 01:14:09,577
I was just sayin' good night.

978
01:14:09,679 --> 01:14:14,139
What is this?
Is this some kind of game to you, James?

979
01:14:14,250 --> 01:14:17,048
- No.
- You don't have to pretend anymore.

980
01:14:17,153 --> 01:14:19,053
You're an amazing girl.

981
01:14:19,155 --> 01:14:23,592
Would you stop it?
Just stop lying to me.

982
01:14:23,693 --> 01:14:27,151
What could I have given you, Sam?
I don't have anything to offer you.

983
01:14:27,263 --> 01:14:29,231
You're the president's daughter,
for Chrissake.

984
01:14:29,332 --> 01:14:31,766
I've spent...

985
01:14:31,868 --> 01:14:35,668
almost my entire life
with people smiling at me...

986
01:14:35,772 --> 01:14:39,833
and laughing at my jokes
and telling me how special I am...

987
01:14:39,943 --> 01:14:45,006
and how great I am
and how nice and smart.

988
01:14:45,114 --> 01:14:48,709
And right now I don't know
if any of that was true.

989
01:14:50,119 --> 01:14:53,953
Maybe it was all some kind
of an act. I don't know.

990
01:14:55,859 --> 01:15:01,126
What if I was different? What if
I was just like everybody else, James?

991
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:05,700
How would you feel about me then?

992
01:15:07,670 --> 01:15:10,230
You just don't get it.
Things aren't different.

993
01:15:10,340 --> 01:15:13,798
What if they were?
I think you owe me at least this.

994
01:15:16,513 --> 01:15:21,314
Forget image.

995
01:15:21,417 --> 01:15:23,851
Forget politics. Forget...

996
01:15:25,221 --> 01:15:29,123
Forget everything else
but who I am right now in here.

997
01:15:34,831 --> 01:15:36,731
If things were different.

998
01:15:38,401 --> 01:15:40,369
If things were different...

999
01:15:42,305 --> 01:15:44,773
I'd still follow you around
all the time...

1000
01:15:46,943 --> 01:15:51,903
because I wanted to,
not because I had to.

1001
01:15:57,654 --> 01:16:00,350
Good night, Sam.

1002
01:16:09,499 --> 01:16:11,467
She's not up yet.

1003
01:16:17,240 --> 01:16:19,140
She's not here.

1004
01:16:22,812 --> 01:16:25,679
Hello. You have reached Moviefone.

1005
01:16:25,782 --> 01:16:29,809
If you know the name of the movie
you'd like to watch, stay on the line.

1006
01:16:29,919 --> 01:16:31,887
Sorry about all the calls.

1007
01:16:31,988 --> 01:16:34,821
Don't worry about it.

1008
01:16:34,924 --> 01:16:39,623
You know, you are quite the photogenic
young lady. I would kill for your ass.

1009
01:16:41,998 --> 01:16:44,193
And Frankie likes it a lot.

1010
01:16:48,438 --> 01:16:49,996
Take a number, buddy.

1011
01:16:50,106 --> 01:16:52,904
Oh. Hey, Liz.

1012
01:16:53,009 --> 01:16:55,569
You have to take this one.

1013
01:17:00,116 --> 01:17:03,244
- Hi. - Sam, your father
is extremely disappointed.

1014
01:17:03,353 --> 01:17:05,321
Is there anything else
we need to know?

1015
01:17:05,421 --> 01:17:07,855
It was just one night, Liz...

1016
01:17:07,957 --> 01:17:12,360
one very... bad night.

1017
01:17:12,462 --> 01:17:15,329
I don't wanna know about your night.
I wanna know about your boyfriend.

1018
01:17:15,431 --> 01:17:18,229
What are you talking about?
Just put him on.

1019
01:17:18,334 --> 01:17:21,269
- Sir, she wants to talk to you.
- I don't wanna talk to her.

1020
01:17:21,371 --> 01:17:23,862
- She went too far this time.
Send in the media rep. - Yes, sir.

1021
01:17:23,973 --> 01:17:25,873
He doesn't want to talk to you, Sam.

1022
01:17:25,975 --> 01:17:29,274
He's there right now, isn't he?
I can hear him.

1023
01:17:29,379 --> 01:17:33,406
- Really, he doesn't. Bye.
- I think he's got some good ideas.

1024
01:17:33,516 --> 01:17:35,484
Sam.

1025
01:17:40,990 --> 01:17:43,254
James.

1026
01:17:48,264 --> 01:17:50,732
- Who are you?
- I'm Agent Dryer, ma'am.

1027
01:17:50,833 --> 01:17:53,233
Mr. Lamson is no longer on this detail.

1028
01:18:06,215 --> 01:18:09,013
So, what does it mean?

1029
01:18:10,153 --> 01:18:12,121
Anyone?

1030
01:18:14,190 --> 01:18:16,158
Anyone?

1031
01:18:17,860 --> 01:18:21,762
At the end of the day,
the prince is... is what?

1032
01:18:21,864 --> 01:18:25,231
- Just a prince.
- Go on.

1033
01:18:26,869 --> 01:18:30,930
Didn't matter how much
he trusted or gave of himself...

1034
01:18:31,040 --> 01:18:33,702
or his possessions.

1035
01:18:33,810 --> 01:18:39,749
At the end of the day,
the prince is and will always be...

1036
01:18:43,720 --> 01:18:45,688
just a prince.

1037
01:18:48,391 --> 01:18:51,827
He'll always be different.

1038
01:18:51,928 --> 01:18:54,192
After Samantha Mackenzie's
table dance last night...

1039
01:18:54,297 --> 01:18:57,027
- a shroud of embarrassment
surrounds the White House today.

1040
01:18:57,133 --> 01:19:00,569
Let's go live to Jeff Michael as he
tells us more about her alleged affair.

1041
01:19:00,670 --> 01:19:02,638
The White House has
no comment regarding...

1042
01:19:02,739 --> 01:19:04,934
a jealous brawl involving
Samantha Mackenzie...

1043
01:19:05,041 --> 01:19:07,942
nor do they have anything to say
about her alleged relationship...

1044
01:19:08,044 --> 01:19:09,944
with one of her
Secret Service agents.

1045
01:19:10,046 --> 01:19:11,946
Reporting live
from Redmond University...

1046
01:19:51,788 --> 01:19:55,053
What are you doing here?

1047
01:19:55,158 --> 01:19:57,183
Well, the question on my mind,
Samantha, is:

1048
01:19:57,293 --> 01:19:58,726
What have you been doing here?

1049
01:20:00,329 --> 01:20:03,355
Been a three-point drop in the polls...

1050
01:20:03,466 --> 01:20:05,730
since your little table dance.

1051
01:20:08,638 --> 01:20:10,538
Is it that bad?

1052
01:20:10,640 --> 01:20:13,905
You've gotta know that we are
in the race of our lives.

1053
01:20:15,011 --> 01:20:17,411
We were elected to set an example.

1054
01:20:17,513 --> 01:20:23,281
They expect more of us.
That's the life we've chosen.

1055
01:20:23,386 --> 01:20:25,854
I didn't choose anything, Mom.

1056
01:20:25,955 --> 01:20:29,891
And I didn't run for anything.
Nobody elected me, remember?

1057
01:20:29,992 --> 01:20:34,452
Like it or not, chosen or not...

1058
01:20:34,564 --> 01:20:37,727
you are the daughter
of the president of the United States.

1059
01:20:37,834 --> 01:20:43,363
Your father and I need you.
Now, we need to be the First Family.

1060
01:20:43,472 --> 01:20:46,032
You want me to leave school?

1061
01:20:49,145 --> 01:20:53,639
When President Harding was elected,
Florence Harding said...

1062
01:20:53,749 --> 01:20:58,948
"Warren, I got you the presidency.
Now what are you gonna do with it?"

1063
01:21:00,289 --> 01:21:03,725
So, let's get your father
the presidency... again...

1064
01:21:03,826 --> 01:21:05,726
see what he does with it.

1065
01:21:06,829 --> 01:21:09,059
It's his time.

1066
01:21:10,166 --> 01:21:12,066
You're asking me to join the campaign?

1067
01:21:12,168 --> 01:21:15,331
Mm-mmm. I'm not asking.

1068
01:22:58,975 --> 01:23:00,943
Good evening, miss.

1069
01:23:05,781 --> 01:23:07,942
I guess you heard,
Samantha Mackenzie raising money...

1070
01:23:08,050 --> 01:23:10,678
for her dad's reelection
one dollar at a time.

1071
01:23:10,786 --> 01:23:14,688
Yes, ladies and gentlemen.
That's... That's the big story.

1072
01:23:14,790 --> 01:23:16,587
Here's the best part.
The Secret Service agent...

1073
01:23:16,692 --> 01:23:19,627
who knocked out the guy at the bar
where Samantha was stripping...

1074
01:23:19,729 --> 01:23:22,289
Turns out, that Secret Service agent
is her boyfriend.

1075
01:23:22,398 --> 01:23:24,298
Ooh!

1076
01:23:24,400 --> 01:23:27,699
And with the help of hard workin' people
like you, we can win this thing.

1077
01:23:27,803 --> 01:23:31,204
Thank you, Motor City!

1078
01:23:31,307 --> 01:23:35,801
Mackenzie!
Mackenzie!

1079
01:23:35,911 --> 01:23:40,814
We're here to discuss your proposed
removal as a disciplinary action.

1080
01:23:40,916 --> 01:23:43,749
Your record is exceptional,
but looking at this report...

1081
01:23:43,853 --> 01:23:46,913
I have my doubts about your ability
to continue as an agent.

1082
01:23:47,023 --> 01:23:49,082
I understand.

1083
01:23:49,191 --> 01:23:52,092
So please tell this panel why we should
allow you to continue as an agent.

1084
01:23:53,863 --> 01:23:55,763
My father was an agent.

1085
01:23:55,865 --> 01:23:59,995
- And my grandfather was before... - But
they're not the ones under review here. You are.

1086
01:24:00,102 --> 01:24:04,129
And if you had a different father or grand-
father, you wouldn't have this opportunity.

1087
01:24:06,475 --> 01:24:10,172
You know, as a little kid...

1088
01:24:10,279 --> 01:24:14,807
I always dreamt about standing on the
sidelines of history, protecting others...

1089
01:24:14,917 --> 01:24:18,182
maybe even the president himself.

1090
01:24:18,287 --> 01:24:24,157
Well, I had the opportunity
to protect a pretty remarkable person.

1091
01:24:24,260 --> 01:24:27,195
Do you have anything to say
to defend your actions?

1092
01:24:27,296 --> 01:24:29,355
You trained me
to expect the unexpected.

1093
01:24:29,465 --> 01:24:34,095
And I tried... not to feel anything.
I tried to keep my distance...

1094
01:24:34,203 --> 01:24:36,103
but I...

1095
01:24:37,206 --> 01:24:40,972
fell deeper... and deeper.

1096
01:24:41,077 --> 01:24:44,376
If having those feelings
means losing my job...

1097
01:24:44,480 --> 01:24:46,277
then that's a loss
I am prepared to take.

1098
01:24:48,117 --> 01:24:53,953
You and I know that mistakes made in our
line of work could mean someone's life.

1099
01:24:55,057 --> 01:24:56,957
So I'm sorry.

1100
01:24:57,059 --> 01:25:00,620
You'll be on suspension
pending your removal...

1101
01:25:00,729 --> 01:25:03,721
and you should start to think
about other alternatives.

1102
01:25:09,004 --> 01:25:12,405
...his humor, his charisma.

1103
01:25:12,508 --> 01:25:14,601
Have we confirmed these numbers?

1104
01:25:14,710 --> 01:25:17,235
And did she sign for them?

1105
01:25:17,346 --> 01:25:20,440
- Well, the only thing...
- Well, that's why we chose this venue.

1106
01:25:20,549 --> 01:25:22,881
- New Hampshire worked, right?
- We're not in New Hampshire anymore.

1107
01:25:22,985 --> 01:25:26,944
- Most people want to hear about
foreign markets. - Pardon me.

1108
01:25:28,891 --> 01:25:31,792
- Hey. How are you doin'?
- Good.

1109
01:25:31,894 --> 01:25:33,862
You okay?

1110
01:25:38,734 --> 01:25:40,964
Sam...

1111
01:25:41,070 --> 01:25:42,970
you're unhappy.

1112
01:25:43,072 --> 01:25:46,200
I get it. But if you're going
to be here, be here.

1113
01:25:46,308 --> 01:25:48,242
Because there's a lot at stake...

1114
01:25:48,344 --> 01:25:51,939
and I really need you to act
like a grown-up right now.

1115
01:25:52,047 --> 01:25:55,642
Obviously, I understand
there is a lot at stake, Dad.

1116
01:25:55,751 --> 01:25:59,551
I have been standing by your side
with Mom my entire life.

1117
01:25:59,655 --> 01:26:01,623
That's why I came home.

1118
01:26:01,724 --> 01:26:05,091
You don't have to tell me how important
it is to be with the people you love.

1119
01:26:05,194 --> 01:26:11,030
I am here. If you want me to be
a grown-up, then you have to allow it.

1120
01:26:21,043 --> 01:26:24,137
- What's goin' on with Sam?
- Uh...

1121
01:26:24,246 --> 01:26:27,147
- What is it?
- Well...

1122
01:26:27,249 --> 01:26:30,741
remember when she was little
and she found that frog...

1123
01:26:30,853 --> 01:26:32,411
and we wouldn't let her keep it...

1124
01:26:32,521 --> 01:26:38,391
and she got that really stubborn little...
unbelievably cute look on her face?

1125
01:26:40,196 --> 01:26:43,495
- Yes.
- She just made that face again.

1126
01:26:45,501 --> 01:26:49,267
Man. Here I am about to go onstage...

1127
01:26:49,371 --> 01:26:51,737
she puts her old man in his place.

1128
01:26:53,409 --> 01:26:56,572
- Really?
- Yeah. Really.

1129
01:26:57,613 --> 01:26:59,979
And?

1130
01:27:00,082 --> 01:27:02,050
And, uh...

1131
01:27:04,220 --> 01:27:07,019
- I dunno. Good for her.
- Will someone get the president?

1132
01:27:07,122 --> 01:27:09,522
It's time to go, Mr. President.
- Ready?

1133
01:27:10,626 --> 01:27:12,992
Let's go.

1134
01:27:13,095 --> 01:27:15,563
And as for our president,
he's gonna do the same thing...

1135
01:27:15,664 --> 01:27:19,498
- to this country that she's done
to her family... embarrass it.

1136
01:27:28,811 --> 01:27:32,474
With all due respect, now that
we�ve just taken direct hits...

1137
01:27:32,581 --> 01:27:34,606
on the domestic agenda, and it's
the last push before the election...

1138
01:27:34,717 --> 01:27:37,481
It's too late to change our position.
I don't think we should address it.

1139
01:27:37,586 --> 01:27:39,383
What do you think, Sam?

1140
01:27:40,656 --> 01:27:43,318
- I don't really have an opinion, Dad.
- Really?

1141
01:27:44,560 --> 01:27:46,460
Are you sure?

1142
01:27:48,297 --> 01:27:54,133
Well, I don't know what could be
more important than home.

1143
01:27:57,773 --> 01:28:00,333
Ladies and gentlemen,
the President of the United States.

1144
01:28:00,442 --> 01:28:02,069
Thanks.

1145
01:28:07,416 --> 01:28:09,384
- Mr. President.
- Mr. President.

1146
01:28:09,485 --> 01:28:10,918
Afternoon, folks.

1147
01:28:22,031 --> 01:28:24,499
Thought you might want a snack.

1148
01:28:27,736 --> 01:28:29,636
Made it myself.

1149
01:28:31,707 --> 01:28:36,906
- Dad.
- Okay, I had that cake made myself.

1150
01:28:46,689 --> 01:28:48,748
How are you doin'?

1151
01:28:50,793 --> 01:28:53,728
- Dad?
- Yeah.

1152
01:28:53,829 --> 01:28:56,297
I need you to make sure
that James is okay.

1153
01:28:59,702 --> 01:29:03,832
He's a good agent.
I'll see what I can do.

1154
01:29:03,939 --> 01:29:06,601
Thank you.

1155
01:29:09,845 --> 01:29:11,745
Did you love him?

1156
01:29:15,050 --> 01:29:17,985
I loved who I got to be with him.

1157
01:29:19,388 --> 01:29:24,451
Even though I didn't do
anything amazing, for me it was.

1158
01:29:27,296 --> 01:29:31,858
I felt like I...
knew myself for the first time.

1159
01:29:34,536 --> 01:29:36,436
Love?

1160
01:29:38,507 --> 01:29:40,907
That too.

1161
01:29:41,009 --> 01:29:43,842
That's what I thought.

1162
01:29:46,048 --> 01:29:48,744
And...
reelected to a second term...

1163
01:29:48,851 --> 01:29:50,842
President John Mackenzie.

1164
01:29:50,953 --> 01:29:56,016
- Thank you very much. God bless the U.S.A.
- We love you, Mac!

1165
01:30:03,766 --> 01:30:09,705
Recently, this...
really fine young woman...

1166
01:30:11,640 --> 01:30:15,235
pointed out to me
the importance of home.

1167
01:30:15,344 --> 01:30:21,180
And, uh, for the next four years,
this administration...

1168
01:30:21,283 --> 01:30:25,481
is going to find its way
back there, starting now.

1169
01:30:25,587 --> 01:30:28,055
Thank you.

1170
01:30:30,959 --> 01:30:32,859
It's your time.

1171
01:30:37,065 --> 01:30:39,727
- The next dance is for you and me.
- Okay.

1172
01:30:41,737 --> 01:30:44,228
What do you think of your father's
policies now, Samantha?

1173
01:30:44,339 --> 01:30:46,307
I have my own policies to think about.

1174
01:31:03,459 --> 01:31:06,485
- It was a nice speech.
- Thanks.

1175
01:31:20,309 --> 01:31:23,574
Dad, one thing you always taught me...

1176
01:31:23,679 --> 01:31:28,275
was to make sure that I'm always at home,
no matter what anyone else thinks.

1177
01:31:28,383 --> 01:31:31,250
It has to include you.

1178
01:32:13,362 --> 01:32:15,830
We all deserve a second chance.

1179
01:32:15,931 --> 01:32:18,525
It's okay.

1180
01:32:24,506 --> 01:32:26,406
Give me your left hand.

1181
01:32:26,508 --> 01:32:28,772
What are you doing?

1182
01:32:28,877 --> 01:32:32,506
Dancing with you.
On my shoulder.

1183
01:32:34,783 --> 01:32:37,479
We shouldn't. We can't.

1184
01:32:37,586 --> 01:32:40,316
Try not to lead this time, okay?

1185
01:34:06,675 --> 01:34:08,643
I, uh...

1186
01:34:10,946 --> 01:34:13,779
believe this is yours.

1187
01:34:13,915 --> 01:34:17,112
It'll take you on your next trip.

1188
01:34:17,219 --> 01:34:19,779
Even included the cooler.

1189
01:34:19,888 --> 01:34:22,413
We did everything
to your exact specifications.

1190
01:34:28,830 --> 01:34:32,561
- Thank you, James.
- Thank you.

1191
01:34:32,668 --> 01:34:35,193
Bye, Sam.

1192
01:34:37,673 --> 01:34:39,641
Now, go try to break a few rules, huh?

1193
01:34:43,345 --> 01:34:45,677
You try to keep some.

1194
01:35:36,898 --> 01:35:38,866
- Forget something?
- Yeah.

1195
01:36:01,523 --> 01:36:04,151
I just forgot my purse.

1196
01:36:13,802 --> 01:36:17,602
- Take good care of him.
- I will.

1197
